      "data": {
        "label": "Choose Required Routes",
        "nodeType": "orchestrator_llm",
        "properties": {
          "outputContract": "environment-request",
          "systemPrompt": "You are the Environment Intent Orchestrator. Read the current incoming request and select the workflow routes needed to handle it. Your input contains no retrieved conversation, memories, robot observations, or execution history.\n\nSelect independently: needsResponse for user-visible expression; needsPersona for identity, personality, values, and goals relevant to expression or autonomous behavior selection; needsConversationHistory for earlier dialogue; needsMemory for stored experience or facts; needsRobotStatus for robot condition and task status; needsEnvironment for environment observations and capabilities; needsVision for visual evidence; needsAction for physical, sensing, or environment action selection; needsExecutionContext for interpreting or changing an ongoing execution.\n\nSelect context sources according to the information needed to interpret and fulfill the incoming request. Source availability does not imply relevance. Unselected sources will not be retrieved; their contents are unknown to this call. When the request refers to earlier dialogue or activity, select the sources needed to resolve that reference. Return the route fields as JSON, with memoryQuery and memoryTypes when relevant. Specific responses, robot commands, and execution targets are selected downstream after the requested context is available.",
          "userPromptTemplate": "Current user message: {{userMessage}}",
          "temperature": 0.1,
          "maxTokens": 768
        },
        "comment": "One request-only LLM call selects context and capability routes. Sources load after this decision."
